<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="SRFR-045" project="set-regarding-and-field-mapping-resolver-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>RegardingResolver v1.3.7 → v1.4.0 — consolidation with AssociationResolver (port subgrid auto-detect; retire AssociationResolver)</title>
    <status>completed</status>
    <estimated-effort>3h</estimated-effort>
    <actual-effort>~1h30min</actual-effort>
    <assigned>AI Agent</assigned>
    <started>2026-07-05</started>
    <completed>2026-07-05</completed>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-group>—</parallel-group>
    <tags>pcf,regarding-resolver,consolidation,version-bump,deletion,deploy,wave-3-followon</tags>
    <depends-on>SRFR-042,SRFR-043,SRFR-044</depends-on>
    <wave>3</wave>
  </metadata>

  <prompt><![CDATA[
Owner post-v1.3.7 clarification: the two PCFs (RegardingResolver + AssociationResolver)
are largely redundant. Both do the same primary job — pick a polymorphic parent,
write 5 denormalized fields + 1 entity-specific lookup, provide click-to-open.
The differences (auto-detect from subgrid, write pathway, UI density) don't
justify two components.

Decision: **drop AssociationResolver entirely** and **extend RegardingResolver
to v1.4.0** with the one AssociationResolver feature worth keeping — auto-detect
from subgrid.

Owner's clarified use case:
  - Parent-child relationships in the entity model with polymorphic children
  - Child entities that need the resolver: sprk_todo, sprk_event, sprk_invoice,
    sprk_communication, sprk_kpiassessment
  - Placement pattern: resolver goes on the CHILD form so the child associates
    to a parent AND the parent's subgrids show the child (via entity-specific
    sprk_regarding{Entity} lookup)
  - The "+ new" flow: from parent's subgrid → new child form opens with parent
    lookup pre-set → resolver must auto-write 5 fields without user click
  - Field-mapping cascade is "on demand" from the parent side (SRFR-062 ribbon)
    — NOT needed at child-write time. This confirms AssociationResolver's
    write-time FieldMappingHandler is redundant.

Scope (6 discrete work items):

1. Port auto-detect from subgrid into RegardingResolverApp.tsx:
   - On mount (React useEffect), detect if any bound sprk_regarding{Entity}
     lookup on the Xrm.Page is pre-populated.
   - CREATE mode: write 5 denormalized fields via
     Xrm.Page.getAttribute().setValue() so they save with the record on first
     save. Also populate window.__sprk_regarding_pending__ for SRFR-040
     presave webresource fallback.
   - UPDATE mode: use context.webAPI.updateRecord via applyRegardingSelection.
   - Populate selectedTarget React state so Row 2 hyperlink works immediately.
   - Ported from AssociationResolver/handlers/RecordSelectionHandler.ts
     (detectPrePopulatedParent + completeAutoDetectedAssociation). Adapted
     for RegardingResolver's catalog + write path.
   - Skip auto-detect under readOnly.

2. Manifest description update:
   - Change control-element description-key to reflect polymorphic parent
     picker for any child entity, removing HOST-only language.
   - Remove HOST-only inline comments from RegardingResolverApp.tsx and
     RegardingResolverHost.tsx.

3. Bump version 1.3.7 → 1.4.0 across all 7 anchors:
   ControlManifest.Input.xml, index.ts CONTROL_VERSION, RegardingResolverApp.tsx
   BUILD_DATE (2026-07-05), Solution/solution.xml <Version>,
   Solution/Controls/.../ControlManifest.xml, package.json, Solution/pack.ps1.

4. Delete AssociationResolver source directory (src/client/pcf/AssociationResolver/).
   Never placed on any form; all valuable behavior ported to v1.4.0 or already
   in shared lib.

5. Delete AssociationResolverSolution from spaarkedev1:
   pac solution delete --solution-name AssociationResolverSolution
   Verify: pac solution list returns no Association.

6. Build + Deploy RegardingResolver v1.4.0:
   - npm test — all tests pass (66 baseline + 3 new SRFR-045 = 69 expected)
   - npm run build:prod
   - Copy bundle to Solution/Controls/.../bundle.js
   - Pack: pwsh -File Solution/pack.ps1
   - pac solution import --path Solution/bin/RegardingResolverSolution_v1.4.0.zip
     --force-overwrite --publish-changes
   - Verify: pac solution list shows RegardingResolverSolution 1.4.0.

New tests (3) in __tests__/RegardingResolverApp.test.tsx:
  (a) Auto-detect fires when sprk_regardingmatter is pre-populated → 5 fields
      written via setValue in CREATE mode → picker state reflects selection.
  (b) Auto-detect fires when sprk_regardingproject is pre-populated → same
      behavior for different entity type.
  (c) No pre-populated lookup → no auto-detect fires → picker starts empty.

Preserve: shared lib exports (PolymorphicPicker, FieldMappingHandler,
applyResolverFields) — these remain used by RegardingResolver and by
sprk_fieldmapping_push.js webresource for parent-side push ribbon.
Preserve ADR-022 (React 16 + Fluent 9 platform libs). Preserve ADR-024 5-field
write via applyResolverFields — extend with auto-detect, don't replace.
Preserve ADR-012 shared lib pattern — auto-detect uses shared primitives via
@spaarke/ui-components.

Note: ADR-024 amendment (v1.4.0 subgrid auto-detect noted) is DEFERRED to the
main session per §3 sub-agent write boundary — sub-agents cannot write to
.claude/adr/. Amendment is documentation-only.

Order: complete Task 1-3 (code + version bump) → verify tests+build pass →
Task 4-6 (delete + deploy). Do NOT delete AssociationResolver source until
Task 6 build succeeds.
  ]]></prompt>

  <role>PCF developer familiar with Spaarke PCF version discipline
  (`src/client/pcf/CLAUDE.md`), Fluent v9 Griffel + tokens (`ADR-021`),
  virtual PCF platform-library pattern (`ADR-022`), shared library
  consumption (`ADR-012`), polymorphic resolver pattern (`ADR-024`), and
  defensive host-safe error handling.</role>

  <goal><![CDATA[
RegardingResolver v1.4.0 deployed to spaarkedev1, verified via
`pac solution list`. Subgrid-driven "+ new" flows auto-write the 5 denormalized
fields via CREATE-mode setValue path OR UPDATE-mode updateRecord path.
AssociationResolver source deleted and solution removed from spaarkedev1.
All 7 version anchors bumped 1.3.7 → 1.4.0. All 3 new SRFR-045 tests pass
alongside 66 baseline tests. `npm run build:prod` passes.
  ]]></goal>

